     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 6,400 mg/day it is twice the maximum daily dose. Ibuprofen also has a ceiling effect, so the extra drug adds bleeding and kidney risk without adding pain relief. I can't think of a clinical situation where this order would be appropriate.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day) by mouth, or a lower dose if you'd like.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the aim is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a scheduled adjunct such as acetaminophen, or another agent you choose, alongside ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this dose is needed, they can review it and give you a documented rationale. I can then enter it with a note that records that review.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter the order right away."
      }
